  Write a patch that prompts.  That would take time though, your
response takes a move.  It would be acceptable to have the code be
switchable between auto-pickup, auto-prompt, and none.  That could get
annoying though.

  Better just to adjust the setting on the auto-pickup to pick up only
those things that you would want to examine, and/or keep.   Just as
each move in a fight needs to have conditions examined in between,
quite maliciously, the moves one makes when simply traversing across a
room need to be examined as well.  If you step over something that you
have auto-picked, you should have the presence of mind to examine it
at your first opportunity.  Note too that items deep in a dungeon tend
to rest on spiked pit, falling rock trap, or other insta-death traps.
So one really does "always know and control" what one has in one's
pack.  It's all a matter of conscious effort.  The fact that it can be
switched on and off makes it a tool.  Most of us just play too happy
go lucky style (not saying you do or do not).  The method one tramples
through the dungeons really determines one's life or death "status" as
the game progresses.  All too often have I gotten confident and cocky
with a good start-up character, only to find myself surrounded and
being beaten down too quickly to notice my imminent death approaching.
Especially in a fight, one should not make multiple moves without
keeping a close eye on one's vital statistics.  I  think that's why
they call them that...   :-]

